INT. PROVINCIAL TAXIDERMY CLUB - MEETING HALL - EVENING

A long, low room paneled in dark wood and ringed with the glass eyes of badgers. A banner says TWENTY-NINTH ANNUAL STUFFED SHIRT AWARDS. A folding table holds a punch bowl and a single plate of deviled eggs.

HORTENSE ABERNATHY-LIU, sixty, club president, in tweed and a name badge, taps a spoon against a glass. She is ignored. CHESTER PUDDIFOOT, seventy, treasurer, mutters into a ledger at the end of the table. And BERNADETTE "BERNIE" OKOYE, forties, the newest member, stands at the deviled eggs with a plastic cup, trying to look as if she has belonged for decades.

HORTENSE
Order. Order, please.

CHESTER
There's nobody here to order, Hortense.

HORTENSE
There are three of us, Chester.

CHESTER
There's two and a half. Bernadette is a guest.

BERNIE
I paid my dues.

CHESTER
You paid half your dues.

BERNIE
I paid the half I could afford.

HORTENSE
That's a fair point.

CHESTER
It's a half point.

Hortense taps the glass again, loudly, and a stuffed owl on the wall falls off its perch and thumps to the carpet. All three look at it. Nobody moves.

BERNIE
Should somebody...?

CHESTER
It's done that before.

HORTENSE
It always lands facing the wall.

The owl lies face-down. Bernie takes a deviled egg, studies it, and sets it down again as if it might be evidence. Chester turns a page of his ledger with enormous care. Hortense straightens her badge.

HORTENSE (CONT'D)
First item. The Stuffed Shirt Award for Excellence in Taxidermy.

CHESTER
Who's nominated?

HORTENSE
Last year's winner was a trout.

BERNIE
Was it a good trout?

CHESTER
It was an adequate trout.

HORTENSE
It was beautiful, Chester.

CHESTER
It had one fin.

HORTENSE
It had one fin when it came to us. We did what we could.

BERNIE
Maybe the fin was the point.

They both look at her. She grips her cup, suddenly aware of herself.

BERNIE (CONT'D)
Like, art. The fin that isn't there.

CHESTER
She has a point.

HORTENSE
She has half a point.

BERNIE
Now you're doing it.

CHESTER
We're a very precise club.

Hortense crosses to the owl, picks it up, and carries it with great tenderness to the table. She sets it between the punch bowl and the eggs.

HORTENSE
This year's winner. By acclamation.

CHESTER
Of whom?

HORTENSE
Of the owl.

CHESTER
It fell off its perch.

HORTENSE
It fell with dignity.

BERNIE
I second it.

CHESTER
You can't second it. You're a guest.

BERNIE
I'm half a member.

CHESTER
(a beat)
Seconded, then.

Hortense produces a small gold ribbon from her handbag and pins it to the owl's chest. She steps back. They stand in a row, Hortense, Chester, and Bernie, looking at the owl, and it looks at the wall.

HORTENSE
A moment of silence.

Nobody speaks. The old radiator knocks twice. Bernie takes the deviled egg after all and eats it.
